	<!-- ================= WARREN DRESS TABLES (migrated from WarrenCarver.cs 2026-08-26;
	     migration itself USER-GREENLIT 2026-08-25, dials CLAUDE unless struck) =================
	     These tables are the warren dress system's DATA: which blueprint, what weight, what
	     spatial hint. The placement LAWS (budgets, one oven per site, one chest per room,
	     articulation guard, re-roll floors, cluster stamps) stay in WarrenCarver.cs, which is
	     the ONLY consumer of these tables. It reads them through PopulationManager's parsed
	     structures and rolls with the carver's own zone-seeded RNG, so warren rebuilds stay
	     deterministic; the engine's Generate path (ambient RNG, Stat.NextULong in
	     XRL.PopulationList.Generate) is deliberately not used.
	     Idioms, all verified in base PopulationTables.xml and the decompile:
	     - Blueprint="*None" is the engine's weighted nothing row (base PopulationTables.xml:6852,
	       PowerGridReplace); the roller interprets the sentinel, nothing spawns.
	     - Hint vocabulary is the engine's own, consumed in our case by WarrenCarver.Seat:
	       Center matches ZoneBuilderSandbox.PlaceObjectInArea's Center (the area centroid);
	       Cleo_TerraFirma_Face is OUR hint (deepest cell from the mouth, the work face) with
	       no engine equivalent, legal here because the engine never reads these tables.
	     - Row ORDER is load-bearing for seed determinism: same seed walks rows in order.
	       Reorder and every warren re-dresses (distribution identical, exact items drift).
	     Weights carry their provenance from the C# tables' comments, copied across verbatim
	     where they existed. Editing weights or adding rows here needs NO recompile.
	     SIM MIRROR: design/warren-lab-v2.html keeps its own JS copies (DRESS, ROOMPOOLS,
	     NATURAL, PLAINTRACE, HALLTABLE + the ITEMS art table, in sim ids). THE SIM LEADS;
	     when a sitting changes dress content, change the sim first and port here. -->

